  "investigation_notes": "Uploads failing \u2014 root cause is dependency `incidentlab-db-1` stopped, not app storage.\n\n* App `incidentlab-app-1` is `running` `Up 5 seconds` (E1) (E6), user `1000:1000` (E6).\n* DB `incidentlab-db-1` is `exited` `Exited (0) 2 seconds ago` (E1), `running: false`, `exit_code: 0`, `oom_killed: false` (E5).\n* App `/health` returns `503` `{\"status\":\"unhealthy\"}` (E2).\n* App logs show `upload` at `/app/main.py line 65` and `health` at `line 113` both fail in `psycopg.connect(DATABASE_URL)` with `psycopg.OperationalError: failed to resolve host 'db': [Errno -3] Temporary failure in name resolution` (E3).\n* Both containers are on network `incidentlab_default` (E5) (E6), app mount `bind` `source: /srv/lab-data` `destination: /data` `rw: true` (E6), so DNS failure is symptom of DB container missing, not misconfiguration.\n* DB logs show `database system is ready to accept connections` at `23:37:00.998` then `received fast shutdown request` at `23:37:08.801`, `aborting any active transactions`, `shutting down`, `checkpoint complete`, `database system is shut down` (E7) \u2014 clean shutdown, no crash.\n* Events show `health_status: healthy` at `23:37:06` then `kill`, `stop`, `die exit 0` for `incidentlab-db-1` at `23:37:08` (E8), with `restart_count: 0` (E5). No OOM, no error (E5).\n* Storage ruled out: `/srv/lab-data` `use_percent: 9.0`, `inode_use_percent: 0.2` (E4); `/` `use_percent: 6.8`, `inode_use_percent: 1.5` (E10).\n* Permissions ruled out: `/srv/lab-data/uploads` `is_dir: true`, `owner 1000:1000`, `mode 0755`, `app 1000:1000`, `app_user_can_write: true` (E9), matching app user (E6).\n\nConclusion: uploads stop because app cannot connect to DB dependency which was cleanly stopped  at `finished_at 2026-10-28T23:37:08.808Z` (E5). Fix requires starting `incidentlab-db-1`, not fixing disk or permissions.\n",
